1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:08,683
FieldRelay is a field-operations console for property maintenance teams, connecting a reported incident, vendor coordination, and a human-authorized dispatch.

2
00:00:08,683 --> 00:00:11,460
This is the deployed FieldRelay application.

3
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:19,258
Evaluators enter with the demo operations account and can explore the working product without credentials or the risk of calling a real person.

4
00:00:19,258 --> 00:00:27,997
Mission Control shows active incidents, recent call tasks, approvals needing attention, dispatch progress, and the call-safety boundaries active in the environment.

5
00:00:27,997 --> 00:00:33,926
When a tenant reports a problem, the operator records its location, category, priority, and description.

6
00:00:33,926 --> 00:00:38,705
FieldRelay assigns a durable identifier and keeps the status visible.

7
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:46,012
Calls and AI Operations then shows each coordination task and its lifecycle instead of hiding phone work in another tool.

8
00:00:46,012 --> 00:00:51,935
Before CALL-E can be contacted, FieldRelay verifies that the contact is authorized for the requested purpose.

9
00:00:51,935 --> 00:00:59,646
It commits the call task and idempotency reservation before any provider request, so a retry cannot silently create duplicate calls.

10
00:00:59,646 --> 00:01:06,161
Only the exact live configuration enables dialing, and the destination number stays inside server-side infrastructure.

11
00:01:06,161 --> 00:01:11,106
The public evaluator environment uses a simulated call adapter and labels it clearly.

12
00:01:11,106 --> 00:01:14,303
This lets judges inspect the complete application safely.

13
00:01:14,303 --> 00:01:25,486
In live mode, CALL-E places the authorized call, gives the disclosure, refers to the incident only by its operational identifier, asks bounded questions, and returns structured data to FieldRelay.

14
00:01:25,486 --> 00:01:37,411
The call-detail screen explains the complete lifecycle: incident, authorized contact, purpose, execution mode, provider state, timeout, attempt count, idempotency key, and audit identity.

15
00:01:37,411 --> 00:01:40,486
FieldRelay accepts only declared answer fields.

16
00:01:40,486 --> 00:01:48,119
This verified live result returned availability yes, a quoted amount of thirty-five dollars, and confidence of zero point eight two.

17
00:01:48,119 --> 00:01:50,685
Transcripts and recordings are not stored.

18
00:01:50,685 --> 00:01:54,988
A quoted cost creates a human decision, not an automatic purchase.

19
00:01:54,988 --> 00:01:59,170
The approval queue shows the evidence, reason, amount, and confidence.

20
00:01:59,170 --> 00:02:02,997
An operator can release, keep pending, or reject the work.

21
00:02:02,997 --> 00:02:10,011
Once approved, the dispatch board tracks the assignment through scheduled, en route, on site, and completed states.

22
00:02:10,011 --> 00:02:12,689
Vendor authorization is equally visible.

23
00:02:12,689 --> 00:02:20,542
Operators review permitted call purposes, regional and language boundaries, contact status, and can revoke authorization without erasing history.

24
00:02:20,542 --> 00:02:24,336
Technicians, analytics, and settings complete the operational picture.

25
00:02:24,336 --> 00:02:29,867
Unmeasured values are described as awaiting evidence instead of being presented as misleading zeroes.

26
00:02:29,867 --> 00:02:34,789
Under the interface, domain rules control the application and infrastructure adapters.

27
00:02:34,789 --> 00:02:37,146
CALL-E is one bounded integration.

28
00:02:37,146 --> 00:02:45,077
Ambiguous outcomes remain unknown and are never automatically redialed; phone numbers and provider payloads never enter the product record.

29
00:02:45,077 --> 00:02:52,511
FieldRelay turns phone coordination into structured, reviewable operations while keeping people in control of cost and dispatch.

30
00:02:52,511 --> 00:02:59,502
The application is live, the source is public, and its reusable CALL-E service-dispatch skill is already merged upstream.
